            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0345" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/15848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-15T18:00:00+02:00">October 15, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>427. The Secretary of the King informs me that the Germans are exerting heavy
                    pressure on King Boris to enter the war.</p>
                <p>He adds the King is doing his best to sidestep the issue and conciliate Germany
                    by making many comparatively unimportant concessions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
